          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %em closed
            if for any pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            can be regarded as forming itself an object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This object is often denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(a,b)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a,b]
            or similar and often addressed as the
            %em
              internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            or simply the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
          %p
            A familiar kind of closed categories are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal categories
            %em closed category
            that does not require the category to already be monoidal. A monoidal structure
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            %em left
            adjoint to the internal-hom, dual to the above characterization of internal-homs as right adjoints to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
          %p
            Although it may seem that in general the closed structure is less intuitive to work with than the monoidal structure, in some cases it is in fact more obvious what the correct internal-homs are than what the correct tensor product is, so the latter was originally defined as an adjoint to the former. This is the case for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray+tensor+product"} Gray tensor product
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+tensor+product"} projective tensor product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            (the original notion of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#basic_definition Basic definition
          %p
            A
            %strong closed category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            together with the following data:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ×
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-] : C^{op} \times C \to C
                = succeed "-functor." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\in C
                called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+object"} unit object
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi C
                        %mo ≅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi I
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\colon Id_C \cong [I,-]
            %li
              %p
                A transformation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_X\colon I \to [X,X]
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extranatural"} extranatural
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                A transformation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mrow
                            %mi Y
                            %mi Z
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^X_{Y Z} \colon  [Y,Z] \to [ [X,Y],[X,Z]]
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                and extranatural in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p which is required to satisfy the following axioms.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The following
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                commutes for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi I
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi j
                                    %mi Y
